sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant SA as Sender application
    participant SS as Sender stack / qdisc
    participant SD as Sender driver
    participant SN as Sender NIC
    participant RN as Receiver NIC
    participant RD as Receiver driver / NAPI
    participant RS as Receiver stack / socket
    participant RA as Receiver application

    Note over RN,RD: Prepare receive capacity before frames arrive
    RD->>RD: Allocate or reuse RX buffers and DMA-map them
    RD->>RN: Publish RX descriptors and notify NIC
    Note over RN,RD: RX descriptors contain buffer DMA addresses and capacities

    Note over SA,SS: If the socket send-memory budget is exhausted, blocking send() waits for space
    SA->>SS: send(): CPU-copy payload into kernel buffers
    SS->>SS: Create skbs and prepare headers and protocol data
    opt Segmentation or IPv4 fragmentation required
        SS->>SS: Prepare output skbs for Ethernet transmission
    end
    SS->>SS: Queue and schedule skbs in qdisc
    Note over SS,SD: Qdisc does not wait for queue space or block the application when full
    Note over SS,SD: Its drop policy may discard an skb and release its references instead
    loop For each outgoing skb representing one Ethernet frame
        Note over SS,SD: tcpdump TX tap on physical interface: after qdisc dequeue, before driver call<br/>Earlier qdisc drops are absent<br/>Capture does not prove wire transmission
        SS->>SD: Hand outgoing skb to driver
        SD->>SD: DMA-map the buffers referenced by skb
        SD->>SN: Publish TX descriptors and notify NIC
        Note over SD,SN: Descriptors contain DMA addresses, lengths and frame boundaries
        SN->>SN: Read TX descriptors and DMA-read host data buffers
        SN->>RN: Transmit Ethernet frame over the link
        RN->>RN: Read RX descriptors and DMA-write into host RX buffers
    end

    par Reclaim sender resources
        SN-->>SD: Report TX completion
        SD->>SD: Reclaim descriptors, remove DMA mappings and release driver skb references
    and Deliver received data
        RN-->>RD: Report RX lengths, boundaries and completion
        RD->>RD: Process completions and build or complete skbs for received data
        RD->>RS: Pass received skbs upward
        RD->>RN: Replenish RX descriptors with available buffers
        Note over RN,RD: Do not overwrite buffers still referenced by the stack
        Note over RD,RS: tcpdump RX tap on physical interface: after driver/NAPI delivery<br/>After software backlog when used, before IP reassembly and TCP/UDP processing<br/>Earlier RX drops are absent<br/>Capture does not prove socket delivery
        RS->>RS: Ethernet decapsulation and IP processing
        opt IPv4 fragments received
            RS->>RS: Reassemble complete IP datagram
        end
        RS->>RS: TCP/UDP processing and destination socket queueing
        RA->>RS: recv(): supply a user buffer
        RS-->>RA: CPU-copy available payload into user buffer
    end
